  "conclusion": "The 448-byte read-ahead already achieves one read per serial control packet. The retained optimization removes impossible receive-policy and optional-deadline branches without changing framing, ownership, timeout renewal, allocation, layout or read count. It improves fixed broker instructions in serial and the three concurrency shapes, improves cycles in the long serial, publishers-32 and large-payload controls, and preserves the complete protocol gates."
